insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'c7d425b7-63cf-4420-abdc-f38a28111259', 'Text\nPart 2: Open Cloze`nFor questions 9–16, read the text below and think of the word which best fits each gap. Use only ONE word in each gap. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → of`n`nText`nThe Popularity of Podcasts`nIn recent years, podcasts have become one (0) ___ the most popular ways to consume information and entertainment. People all over the world listen to them while commuting, exercising, or simply relaxing at home.`nOne reason for their success is the wide range of topics available. There is a podcast for almost every interest, (9) ___ politics and science to comedy and storytelling. This variety makes it easy for listeners to find content that suits their preferences.`nAnother advantage is convenience. Unlike traditional radio, podcasts can be listened to at any time, depending (10) ___ the listener’s schedule. This flexibility has made them particularly appealing to busy individuals.`nIn addition, many podcasts are free, which allows people to access high-quality content without having to pay (11) ___. This has helped increase their popularity even further.`nHowever, producing a successful podcast requires more (12) ___ just a good idea. Creators need to plan their episodes carefully and ensure that the content is engaging enough to keep listeners interested.`nIt is also important to promote the podcast effectively. Without proper marketing, even the best content may go unnoticed (13) ___ the large number of podcasts available today.`nDespite these challenges, many people continue to create podcasts because they enjoy sharing their ideas and connecting (14) ___ others. For some, it even becomes a full-time job.`nOverall, podcasts have changed the way people consume media, and they are likely to remain popular for years to come. As technology continues to improve, their influence is expected to grow even (15) ___.`n`nQuestions`n9 ______10 ______11 ______12 ______13 ______14 ______15 ______16 ______`n`nAnswer Key`n9 from10 on11 anything12 than13 among14 with15 further16 ahead (Nota: este último puede variar según interpretación, pero “ahead” encaja como cierre natural)`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'c7d425b7-63cf-4420-abdc-f38a28111259', 'Text\nPart 2: Open Cloze`nFor questions 9–16, read the text below and think of the word which best fits each gap. Use only ONE word in each gap. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → for`n`nText`nThe Benefits of Spending Time Outdoors`nIn today’s modern world, many people spend most (0) ___ their time indoors, often in front of screens. However, research shows that spending time outside can be extremely beneficial for both physical and mental health.`nOne of the main advantages is that being in nature helps reduce stress. People who regularly go (9) ___ walks in parks or forests often feel more relaxed and positive.`nFresh air and natural light also play an important role (10) ___ improving overall well-being. Sunlight, for example, helps the body produce vitamin D, which is essential (11) ___ maintaining strong bones.`nIn addition, outdoor activities can encourage people to be more active. Instead (12) ___ sitting for long periods, they may choose to walk, cycle, or take part in sports.`nAnother benefit is the opportunity to disconnect (13) ___ technology. Taking a break from devices allows individuals to focus (14) ___ the present moment and enjoy their surroundings.`nSpending time outdoors can also have social benefits. People often meet friends or family members outside, which helps them stay connected (15) ___ others.`nOverall, even a short amount of time spent in nature can make a significant difference. It is clear that going outside regularly is something everyone should try to include (16) ___ their daily routine.`n`nQuestions`n9 ______10 ______11 ______12 ______13 ______14 ______15 ______16 ______`n`nAnswer Key`n9 for10 in11 for12 of13 from14 on15 with16 in`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'c7d425b7-63cf-4420-abdc-f38a28111259', 'Text\nPart 2: Open Cloze`nFor questions 9–16, read the text below and think of the word which best fits each gap. Use only ONE word in each gap. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → in`n`nText`nLearning Through Travel`nTravelling is often seen as a way to relax, but it can also result (0) ___ valuable learning experiences. Visiting new places allows people to discover different cultures, traditions and ways of life.`nOne of the main advantages of travelling is the opportunity to learn (9) ___ other people. By interacting with locals, travellers can gain a deeper understanding of the country they are visiting.`nIn addition, travel encourages people to step (10) ___ of their comfort zones. This can be challenging at first, but it often leads to personal growth and increased confidence.`nAnother benefit is the chance to practise languages. Being surrounded (11) ___ native speakers gives travellers the opportunity to improve their communication skills much faster (12) ___ in a classroom.`nTravelling also teaches important life skills, such (13) ___ problem-solving and adaptability. Unexpected situations may arise, and travellers must find ways to deal (14) ___ them effectively.`nFurthermore, experiencing different cultures helps people become more open-minded. They begin to see things (15) ___ different perspectives and develop greater respect for others.`nOverall, travel is much more than just a holiday. It is a powerful way to learn about the world and about oneself, and it can have a lasting impact (16) ___ a person’s life.`n`nQuestions`n9 ______10 ______11 ______12 ______13 ______14 ______15 ______16 ______`n`nAnswer Key`n9 from10 out11 by12 than13 as14 with15 from16 on`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'c7d425b7-63cf-4420-abdc-f38a28111259', 'Text\nB2 First (FCE) – Use of English`nPart 2: Open Cloze`nFor questions 9–16, read the text below and think of the word which best fits each gap. Use only ONE word in each gap. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → on`n`nText`nThe Influence of Social Media`nSocial media has had a major impact (0) ___ the way people communicate in recent years. It allows individuals to share information instantly and stay connected with others around the world.`nOne of the main reasons (9) ___ its popularity is that it is easy to use and widely accessible. Most people can create an account and start sharing content within minutes.`nHowever, social media is not without its drawbacks. Some users spend too much time (10) ___ their devices, which can affect their daily routines and productivity.`nAnother issue is the pressure to present a perfect image online. People often compare themselves (11) ___ others, which can lead to feelings of insecurity.`nDespite these disadvantages, social media can also be used (12) ___ a positive way. It provides a platform for raising awareness about important issues and connecting people with similar interests.`nIn addition, many businesses rely (13) ___ social media to promote their products and reach a wider audience. This has changed the way companies interact with customers.`nIt is important for users to be aware (14) ___ how they use social media and to set limits if necessary. Maintaining a healthy balance between online and offline life is essential.`nOverall, social media is a powerful tool that can have both positive and negative effects. The key is to use it wisely and take advantage (15) ___ its benefits without letting it take control (16) ___ your time.`n`nQuestions`n9 ______10 ______11 ______12 ______13 ______14 ______15 ______16 ______`n`nAnswer Key`n9 for10 on11 with12 in13 on14 of15 of16 of`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'c7d425b7-63cf-4420-abdc-f38a28111259', 'Text\nB2 First (FCE) – Use of English`nPart 2: Open Cloze`nFor questions 9–16, read the text below and think of the word which best fits each gap. Use only ONE word in each gap. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → to`n`nText`nThe Value of Teamwork`nWorking with others is an essential skill in both education and professional life. Many tasks are too complex for one person to complete alone, which is why teamwork plays such an important role (0) ___ achieving success.`nOne of the main advantages of teamwork is that it allows people to benefit (9) ___ each other’s strengths. Every member of a group can contribute different skills and ideas.`nIn addition, working in a team often leads (10) ___ more creative solutions. When people share their opinions, they can build (11) ___ each other’s suggestions and develop better results.`nHowever, teamwork can also present challenges. For example, disagreements may arise, and it is important to deal (12) ___ them in a respectful way.`nCommunication is key to effective teamwork. Without clear communication, it is easy (13) ___ misunderstand instructions or expectations, which can cause problems within the group.`nAnother important aspect is responsibility. Each member must carry (14) ___ their part of the work in order for the team to succeed.`nTrust is also essential. Team members need to rely (15) ___ one another and feel confident that everyone is working towards the same goal.`nOverall, teamwork is a valuable skill that can lead (16) ___ better outcomes and stronger relationships when managed effectively.`n`nQuestions`n9 ______10 ______11 ______12 ______13 ______14 ______15 ______16 ______`n`nAnswer Key`n9 from10 to11 on12 with13 to14 out15 on16 to`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '1c4186d0-fdbe-41e7-8266-efdf712c3006', 'Text\nPart 3: Word Formation`nFor questions 17–24, read the text below. Use the word given in capitals at the end of some of the lines to form a word that fits in the gap in the same line. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → useful (USE)`n`nText`nThe Advantages of Volunteering`nVolunteering is becoming increasingly popular, especially among young people who are looking for (0) ___ experiences. (USE)`nOne of the main benefits of volunteering is the opportunity for personal (17) ___. It allows individuals to learn new skills and gain confidence. (DEVELOP)`nIn addition, volunteering can improve your (18) ___ skills, as you often need to work with people from different backgrounds. (COMMUNICATE)`nMany organisations depend on the (19) ___ of volunteers to continue their work. Without them, it would be difficult to provide support to those in need. (CONTRIBUTE)`nAnother advantage is that volunteering can be extremely (20) ___. Helping others often brings a sense of satisfaction and purpose. (REWARD)`nMoreover, it can increase your (21) ___ when applying for jobs, as employers value candidates with experience in teamwork and responsibility. (EMPLOY)`nHowever, it is important to choose the right type of volunteering. If the activity is not (22) ___ for you, it may become less enjoyable over time. (SUIT)`nVolunteers must also be (23) ___ and committed, as organisations rely on them to carry out important tasks. (RELY)`nIn conclusion, volunteering is a highly (24) ___ activity that can benefit both individuals and society as a whole. (VALUE)`n`nAnswer Key`n17 development18 communication19 contribution20 rewarding21 employability22 suitable23 reliable24 valuable`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '1c4186d0-fdbe-41e7-8266-efdf712c3006', 'Text\nPart 3: Word Formation`nFor questions 17–24, read the text below. Use the word given in capitals at the end of some of the lines to form a word that fits in the gap in the same line. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → successful (SUCCESS)`n`nText`nThe Growth of Urban Cycling`nIn recent years, cycling in cities has become increasingly (0) ___ as more people look for alternative ways of travelling. (SUCCESS)`nOne of the main reasons for this trend is the growing (17) ___ of environmental issues. People are becoming more concerned about pollution and climate change. (AWARE)`nCycling is also a (18) ___ form of transport, as it does not require fuel and has low maintenance costs. (COST)`nIn addition, many cities have made improvements to their infrastructure to ensure the (19) ___ of cyclists. This includes building dedicated bike lanes and improving road conditions. (SAFE)`nAnother advantage is the positive effect on health. Regular cycling can lead to significant (20) ___ in physical fitness and overall well-being. (IMPROVE)`nHowever, there are still some challenges. In certain areas, cycling can be (21) ___ due to heavy traffic or poor road design. (DANGER)`nTo address these issues, governments need to invest in better facilities and encourage more (22) ___ participation in cycling programmes. (WIDE)`nPublic campaigns can also help change people''s attitudes and increase the (23) ___ of cycling as a daily activity. (POPULAR)`nOverall, urban cycling is a (24) ___ solution that benefits both individuals and the environment. (PRACTICE)`n`nAnswer Key`n17 awareness18 cost-effective (también se acepta “costly” en negativo, pero aquí encaja mejor “cost-effective”)19 safety20 improvement21 dangerous22 widespread23 popularity24 practical`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '1c4186d0-fdbe-41e7-8266-efdf712c3006', 'Text\nPart 3: Word Formation`nFor questions 17–24, read the text below. Use the word given in capitals at the end of some of the lines to form a word that fits in the gap in the same line. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → healthy (HEALTH)`n`nText`nThe Impact of Technology on Education`nTechnology has had a significant impact on modern education, making learning more (0) ___ and accessible than ever before. (HEALTH)`nOne of the main advantages is the (17) ___ of online resources. Students can access information quickly and easily from almost anywhere. (AVAILABLE)`nIn addition, digital tools allow for greater (18) ___ in the classroom. Teachers can use videos, apps and interactive materials to engage students. (CREATE)`nAnother benefit is the (19) ___ of learning methods. Technology enables teachers to adapt their lessons to suit different learning styles. (VARIOUS)`nHowever, there are also some (20) ___. Not all students have equal access to technology, which can create inequality. (ADVANTAGE)`nFurthermore, excessive use of devices can lead to (21) ___ and reduced concentration. (DISTRACT)`nIt is also important to consider the role of teachers. While technology can be helpful, it cannot replace human (22) ___ and guidance. (INTERACT)`nSchools must find a balance between using technology and maintaining traditional teaching methods. This requires careful (23) ___ and planning. (DECIDE)`nIn conclusion, technology has brought many changes to education, and its influence is likely to continue growing. However, its use must be (24) ___ managed to ensure the best results for students. (CARE)`n`nAnswer Key`n17 availability18 creativity19 variety20 disadvantages21 distraction22 interaction23 decision-making (también se acepta “decisions” dependiendo del enfoque)24 carefully`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '1c4186d0-fdbe-41e7-8266-efdf712c3006', 'Text\nPart 3: Word Formation`nFor questions 17–24, read the text below. Use the word given in capitals at the end of some of the lines to form a word that fits in the gap in the same line. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → different (DIFFER)`n`nText`nThe Role of Music in Everyday Life`nMusic plays an important role in people’s lives and can have a powerful effect on our emotions. People listen to music for many (0) ___ reasons, depending on their mood and preferences. (DIFFER)`nOne of the main benefits of music is its ability to provide (17) ___. Listening to your favourite songs can help you relax after a stressful day. (ENJOY)`nIn addition, music can improve (18) ___ by helping people remember information more easily. For this reason, it is sometimes used as a learning tool. (MEMBER)`nMusic also has a strong social aspect. Concerts and festivals bring people together and create a sense of (19) ___ among participants. (COMMUNE)`nFor some individuals, music is more than just entertainment. It can become a (20) ___ career, allowing them to express their creativity. (PROFESSION)`nHowever, not all effects of music are positive. Listening to loud music for long periods can be (21) ___ to your hearing. (HARM)`nIt is important to be (22) ___ of how often and how loudly you listen to music. Taking breaks can help reduce the risk of damage. (CARE)`nAnother interesting point is the (23) ___ of music across cultures. Every country has its own musical traditions and styles. (VARY)`nIn conclusion, music is a highly (24) ___ part of human life that influences people in many different ways. (VALUE)`n`nAnswer Key`n17 enjoyment18 memory19 community20 professional21 harmful22 careful23 variety24 valuable`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '1c4186d0-fdbe-41e7-8266-efdf712c3006', 'Text\nPart 3: Word Formation`nFor questions 17–24, read the text below. Use the word given in capitals at the end of some of the lines to form a word that fits in the gap in the same line. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0 → natural (NATURE)`n`nText`nThe Importance of Time Management`nManaging time effectively is an essential skill in modern life. It helps people stay organised and increases their (0) ___ in both work and study. (NATURE)`nOne of the main benefits of good time management is improved (17) ___. By planning tasks carefully, individuals can complete their work more efficiently. (PRODUCT)`nIn addition, it reduces stress. When people feel in control of their schedule, they are less likely to experience (18) ___. (ANXIOUS)`nAnother advantage is better decision-making. Having enough time allows individuals to think more (19) ___ before taking action. (CARE)`nHowever, poor time management can lead to serious problems. For example, it may result in missed deadlines and a lack of (20) ___. (RESPONSIBLE)`nTo avoid these issues, it is important to set clear goals and priorities. This requires a high level of (21) ___ and focus. (DISCIPLINE)`nUsing tools such as calendars and to-do lists can also be (22) ___. They help people keep track of their tasks and deadlines. (HELP)`nIn addition, it is important to remain flexible. Unexpected situations may require quick (23) ___ to plans. (ADJUST)`nIn conclusion, time management is a highly (24) ___ skill that can lead to greater success and a better quality of life. (VALUE)`n`nAnswer Key`n17 productivity18 anxiety19 carefully20 responsibility21 discipline22 helpful23 adjustments24 valuable`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'd02d4a2a-734c-4a46-8c7e-7b95734ee84d', 'Text\nPart 4: Key Word Transformations`nFor questions 25–30, complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0I last saw him two years ago.seen`nI haven’t __________________ him for two years.`nAnswer: seen`n`nQuestions`n25It was not necessary for me to wake up early yesterday.have`nI __________________ wake up early yesterday.`n`n26“Don’t forget to send the email,” she told me.reminded`nShe __________________ the email.`n`n27This is the best restaurant I have ever been to.never`nI __________________ a better restaurant than this one.`n`n28They are repairing the road outside my house.being`nThe road outside my house __________________ repaired.`n`n29I regret not studying harder for the exam.wish`nI __________________ harder for the exam.`n`n30It is possible that he will arrive late.may`nHe __________________ late.`n`nAnswer Key`n25 didn’t have to26 reminded me to send27 have never been to28 is being29 wish I had studied30 may arrive`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'd02d4a2a-734c-4a46-8c7e-7b95734ee84d', 'Text\nPart 4: Key Word Transformations`nFor questions 25–30, complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0She started working here three years ago.for`nShe has __________________ here for three years.`nAnswer: worked`n`nQuestions`n25I don’t think this book is interesting.find`nI __________________ interesting.`n`n26“You should try the new restaurant,” he said to us.advised`nHe __________________ the new restaurant.`n`n27It was too cold for us to go swimming.enough`nIt wasn’t __________________ for us to go swimming.`n`n28Someone has stolen my bike.been`nMy bike __________________ stolen.`n`n29I haven’t spoken to her for a month.last`nThe __________________ her was a month ago.`n`n30He is too young to drive a car.old`nHe isn’t __________________ drive a car.`n`nAnswer Key`n25 don’t find this book26 advised us to try27 warm enough28 has been29 last time I spoke to30 old enough to`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'd02d4a2a-734c-4a46-8c7e-7b95734ee84d', 'Text\nPart 4: Key Word Transformations`nFor questions 25–30, complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0They moved to this city five years ago.since`nThey have lived in this city __________________ five years.`nAnswer: since`n`nQuestions`n25I didn’t expect the exam to be so difficult.than`nThe exam was __________________ I expected.`n`n26“Let’s go to the cinema tonight,” he said.suggested`nHe __________________ to the cinema that night.`n`n27It is not necessary to bring your own food.have`nYou __________________ bring your own food.`n`n28People believe that the company will open a new office.is`nThe company __________________ open a new office.`n`n29I started learning English when I was six.been`nI __________________ English since I was six.`n`n30The last time I saw him was at the party.since`nI __________________ him since the party.`n`nAnswer Key`n25 more difficult than26 suggested going27 don’t have to28 is believed to29 have been learning30 haven’t seen`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'd02d4a2a-734c-4a46-8c7e-7b95734ee84d', 'Text\nPart 4: Key Word Transformations`nFor questions 25–30, complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0I began reading this book last week.been`nI have __________________ this book since last week.`nAnswer: been reading`n`nQuestions`n25It’s possible that they missed the train.might`nThey __________________ the train.`n`n26“You must finish your homework today,” the teacher said.told`nThe teacher __________________ homework that day.`n`n27This jacket is too small for me.enough`nThis jacket __________________ for me.`n`n28I last visited my grandparents two months ago.for`nI __________________ my grandparents for two months.`n`n29Learning Spanish is not as difficult as I expected.than`nLearning Spanish is __________________ I expected.`n`n30They will probably announce the results tomorrow.likely`nThe results __________________ announced tomorrow.`n`nAnswer Key`n25 might have missed26 told me to finish my27 isn’t big enough28 haven’t visited29 less difficult than30 are likely to be`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'd02d4a2a-734c-4a46-8c7e-7b95734ee84d', 'Text\nPart 4: Key Word Transformations`nFor questions 25–30, complete the second sentence so that it has a similar meaning to the first sentence, using the word given. Do not change the word given. You must use between two and five words, including the word given. There is an example at the beginning (0).`n`nExample:`n0He started playing football when he was ten.since`nHe has played football __________________ he was ten.`nAnswer: since`n`nQuestions`n25I don’t think she will pass the exam.unlikely`nShe __________________ pass the exam.`n`n26“Why don’t we go for a walk?” she said.suggested`nShe __________________ for a walk.`n`n27It took me three hours to finish the project.spent`nI __________________ the project.`n`n28Someone is cleaning the office at the moment.being`nThe office __________________ at the moment.`n`n29I regret telling him the truth.wish`nI __________________ him the truth.`n`n30It isn’t necessary to buy tickets in advance.need`nYou __________________ tickets in advance.`n`nAnswer Key`n25 is unlikely to26 suggested going27 spent three hours finishing28 is being cleaned29 wish I hadn’t told30 don’t need to buy`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '6f873582-07bf-436a-9a25-492b748678c7', 'Text\nPart 5 – Multiple Choice`nYou are going to read a text about learning new skills. For questions 31–36, choose the answer (A, B, C or D) which you think fits best according to the text.`n`nThe Challenge of Learning Something New`nMany people believe that learning new skills becomes increasingly difficult with age. While it is true that children often pick up new abilities more quickly, research suggests that adults have their own advantages when it comes to learning.`nOne reason adults may struggle is that they tend to be more afraid of making mistakes. Unlike children, who often learn through trial and error without worrying about failure, adults can become discouraged if they do not succeed immediately. This fear can slow down the learning process, as it prevents them from experimenting freely.`nHowever, adults usually have better concentration and are more motivated. They often choose to learn skills that are directly relevant to their personal or professional lives. For example, someone might learn a new language to improve their job opportunities or take up cooking to lead a healthier lifestyle. This clear purpose can make learning more effective.`nAnother advantage adults have is their ability to connect new information with existing knowledge. Because they have more life experience, they can relate what they are learning to something they already understand. This can help them grasp complex ideas more easily than younger learners.`nOn the other hand, adults may have less time to dedicate to learning. Responsibilities such as work and family can limit the hours available for practice. As a result, progress may appear slower, even if the quality of learning is high.`nExperts suggest that the best approach for adult learners is to focus on consistency rather than speed. Short, regular practice sessions are more effective than occasional long ones. In addition, creating a supportive environment and setting realistic goals can help maintain motivation over time.`nIn conclusion, although adults may face certain challenges when learning new skills, they also possess strengths that can lead to success. With the right strategies, learning can remain a rewarding experience at any age.`n`nQuestions`n31. What is the writer’s main point in the first paragraph?`nA. Children are better learners than adults in every wayB. Adults and children learn differently, but both have advantagesC. Adults should not try to learn new skillsD. Learning becomes impossible after a certain age`n`n32. Why do adults sometimes learn more slowly than children?`nA. They have less intelligenceB. They lack interest in learningC. They are afraid of making mistakesD. They prefer learning alone`n`n33. What helps adults learn more effectively according to the text?`nA. Having a clear reason for learningB. Competing with other learnersC. Avoiding difficult subjectsD. Studying for long hours every day`n`n34. What advantage do adults have because of their experience?`nA. They can memorise information fasterB. They need less practiceC. They can connect new ideas to what they already knowD. They understand everything immediately`n`n35. Why might adults seem to make slower progress?`nA. They are less capable than childrenB. They forget information quicklyC. They have limited time to practiseD. They choose difficult topics`n`n36. What does the writer suggest is the best way for adults to learn?`nA. Studying as quickly as possibleB. Practising regularly in short sessionsC. Learning only with teachersD. Avoiding challenging material`n`nAnswer Key`nB `nC `nA `nC `nC `nB`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '6f873582-07bf-436a-9a25-492b748678c7', 'Text\nPart 5 – Multiple Choice`nYou are going to read a text about remote working. For questions 31–36, choose the answer (A, B, C or D) which you think fits best according to the text.`n`nThe Rise of Remote Work`nIn recent years, remote work has become increasingly popular, changing the way many people approach their jobs. Advances in technology have made it possible for employees to work from almost anywhere, as long as they have access to a computer and a stable internet connection. While this shift offers many benefits, it also presents certain challenges.`nOne of the main advantages of remote work is flexibility. Employees can often choose their working hours, which allows them to balance their professional and personal lives more effectively. For instance, some people may prefer to start work early in the morning, while others feel more productive later in the day. This flexibility can lead to higher job satisfaction and improved well-being.`nHowever, working from home can also create difficulties. One common problem is the lack of clear boundaries between work and personal life. Without a physical separation, such as an office, some workers find it hard to switch off at the end of the day. This can result in longer working hours and increased stress.`nCommunication is another important issue. In a traditional office, employees can easily share ideas and ask questions in person. In contrast, remote workers rely on emails, messages, or video calls. Although these tools are useful, they may sometimes lead to misunderstandings or delays in communication.`nDespite these challenges, many companies have recognised the advantages of remote work. They have found that employees can be just as productive, or even more so, when working from home. Additionally, businesses can reduce costs by needing less office space.`nExperts suggest that successful remote workers develop good habits, such as setting a daily routine and creating a dedicated workspace. These strategies can help maintain focus and improve efficiency.`nOverall, remote work is likely to remain an important part of modern life. By understanding both its benefits and its drawbacks, individuals and organisations can make the most of this way of working.`n`nQuestions`n31. What is the main idea of the first paragraph?`nA. Remote work is only possible for certain jobsB. Technology has made remote work more commonC. Most people prefer working in officesD. Remote work is a recent failure`n`n32. What is one benefit of remote work mentioned in the text?`nA. Employees earn more moneyB. Workers have more control over their schedulesC. People work fewer hoursD. Companies provide better equipment`n`n33. What problem do some remote workers experience?`nA. They cannot communicate with colleaguesB. They lose interest in their workC. They find it difficult to separate work from personal lifeD. They are unable to use technology`n`n34. Why can communication be challenging in remote work?`nA. Workers do not like using digital toolsB. Messages can sometimes be unclear or slowC. Employees refuse to communicateD. Video calls are too expensive`n`n35. What have companies discovered about remote work?`nA. It always reduces productivityB. Employees cannot work independentlyC. It can maintain or increase productivityD. It is too expensive to organise`n`n36. What does the writer recommend for remote workers?`nA. Working without a scheduleB. Avoiding communication with colleaguesC. Creating routines and a specific workspaceD. Changing jobs regularly`n`nAnswer Key`nB `nB `nC `nB `nC `nC`n`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '6f873582-07bf-436a-9a25-492b748678c7', 'Text\nPart 5 – Multiple Choice`nYou are going to read a text about the impact of social media. For questions 31–36, choose the answer (A, B, C or D) which you think fits best according to the text.`n`nThe Influence of Social Media on Daily Life`nOver the past decade, social media has become an essential part of everyday life for millions of people around the world. Platforms that allow users to share photos, videos, and messages have transformed the way individuals communicate and interact. While these changes have brought many positive effects, they have also raised some concerns.`nOne clear benefit of social media is the ability to stay connected with others. People can easily communicate with friends and family, even if they live far away. In addition, social media allows users to meet new people who share similar interests, which can lead to the creation of online communities.`nHowever, the widespread use of social media has also led to certain problems. For example, some users may spend too much time online, which can reduce the amount of time they dedicate to other activities such as studying, exercising, or socialising in person. This can negatively affect both physical and mental health.`nAnother issue is the way people present themselves online. Many users only share the most positive aspects of their lives, creating an unrealistic image. As a result, others may compare themselves to these idealised versions and feel dissatisfied with their own lives.`nDespite these drawbacks, social media can also be a powerful tool for learning and awareness. Educational content is widely available, and users can quickly access information on a variety of topics. Furthermore, social media has been used to raise awareness about important global issues.`nExperts recommend using social media in a balanced way. Setting time limits and being aware of how online content affects emotions can help users avoid negative experiences. By using these platforms responsibly, individuals can enjoy their benefits while reducing potential risks.`nIn conclusion, social media plays a significant role in modern society. Although it presents challenges, it also offers valuable opportunities when used carefully.`n`nQuestions`n31. What is the main idea of the first paragraph?`nA. Social media is only used for entertainmentB. Social media has changed communication and interactionC. People no longer communicate in real lifeD. Social media is unpopular today`n`n32. What is one advantage of social media mentioned in the text?`nA. It replaces face-to-face communication completelyB. It helps people stay in contact with othersC. It improves people’s physical healthD. It limits communication`n`n33. What problem related to time does the writer mention?`nA. People cannot access social media easilyB. Users spend too little time onlineC. People may spend too much time using social mediaD. Social media reduces working hours`n`n34. Why can social media affect people’s self-image?`nA. Users share only negative experiencesB. People compare themselves to unrealistic contentC. Social media shows real life exactly as it isD. Users do not look at other profiles`n`n35. What positive use of social media is highlighted?`nA. It reduces global problemsB. It replaces traditional educationC. It provides access to information and raises awarenessD. It eliminates the need for teachers`n`n36. What does the writer suggest users should do?`nA. Stop using social media completelyB. Use social media without limitsC. Use social media carefully and in moderationD. Only use social media for work`n`nAnswer Key`nB `nB `nC `nB `nC `nC `n`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '6f873582-07bf-436a-9a25-492b748678c7', 'Text\nPart 5 – Multiple Choice`nYou are going to read a text about the importance of hobbies. For questions 31–36, choose the answer (A, B, C or D) which you think fits best according to the text.`n`nWhy Hobbies Matter More Than You Think`nIn today’s busy world, many people focus most of their time on work or studies, often forgetting the importance of hobbies. However, having an activity that you enjoy in your free time can bring significant benefits to both your mental and physical health.`nOne of the main advantages of hobbies is that they help reduce stress. After a long day, engaging in a relaxing or enjoyable activity can help people disconnect from their responsibilities. Whether it is painting, gardening, or playing a musical instrument, hobbies allow individuals to focus on something positive and creative.`nIn addition, hobbies can help people develop new skills. For example, someone who starts cooking as a hobby may improve their ability to prepare healthy meals. Others might learn practical skills such as repairing objects or managing their time more effectively. These abilities can sometimes even be useful in professional situations.`nHobbies can also play an important role in social life. Joining clubs or groups related to a particular interest can help people meet others with similar passions. This can be especially valuable for those who find it difficult to make friends in other situations.`nDespite these benefits, some people feel they do not have enough time for hobbies. Busy schedules and daily responsibilities can make it difficult to find free time. However, experts suggest that even short periods of time dedicated to hobbies can be beneficial.`nAnother common misunderstanding is that hobbies must be expensive or require special talent. In reality, many enjoyable activities are simple and affordable. Reading, walking, or writing are examples of hobbies that do not require significant resources.`nIn conclusion, hobbies are not just a way to pass the time. They can improve well-being, develop useful skills, and strengthen social connections. Making time for them, even in a busy life, can have a positive impact.`n`nQuestions`n31. What is the writer’s main point in the first paragraph?`nA. People should stop working so muchB. Hobbies are not important in modern lifeC. Hobbies are often forgotten but are beneficialD. Only students need hobbies`n`n32. How do hobbies help reduce stress?`nA. They make people more productiveB. They allow people to focus on enjoyable activitiesC. They increase responsibilitiesD. They require a lot of effort`n`n33. What is one benefit of hobbies mentioned in relation to skills?`nA. They guarantee better jobsB. They help people learn useful abilitiesC. They replace formal educationD. They are only useful for professionals`n`n34. How can hobbies improve social life?`nA. By helping people meet others with similar interestsB. By reducing communicationC. By encouraging people to work aloneD. By limiting free time`n`n35. Why do some people avoid having hobbies?`nA. They think hobbies are boringB. They believe hobbies are only for childrenC. They feel they do not have enough timeD. They do not understand hobbies`n`n36. What does the writer say about hobbies and cost?`nA. All hobbies are expensiveB. Only talented people can have hobbiesC. Hobbies usually require special equipmentD. Many hobbies are simple and affordable`n`nAnswer Key`nC `nB `nB `nA `nC `nD`n`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', '6f873582-07bf-436a-9a25-492b748678c7', 'Text\nPart 5 – Multiple Choice`nYou are going to read a text about living in cities. For questions 31–36, choose the answer (A, B, C or D) which you think fits best according to the text.`n`nCity Life: Advantages and Challenges`nFor many people, living in a large city is an exciting and attractive option. Cities offer a wide range of opportunities, from career possibilities to entertainment and cultural experiences. However, city life also comes with certain disadvantages that can affect people’s quality of life.`nOne of the biggest advantages of living in a city is access to employment. Large cities usually have more job opportunities and a greater variety of industries. This makes it easier for people to find work that suits their skills and interests. In addition, cities often offer better public services, such as education and healthcare.`nAnother positive aspect is the variety of activities available. Residents can enjoy museums, theatres, restaurants, and sporting events. This means there is always something to do, regardless of personal interests. For many, this makes city life more dynamic and enjoyable.`nOn the other hand, living in a city can be expensive. Housing costs are often much higher than in smaller towns or rural areas. As a result, many people have to spend a large part of their income on rent or mortgages. This financial pressure can reduce the overall benefits of city living.`nTraffic and pollution are also common problems in urban areas. Heavy traffic can make daily travel stressful and time-consuming. At the same time, air pollution can have a negative impact on people’s health, especially for those who live in highly populated areas.`nDespite these challenges, many people continue to choose city life. Some believe that the opportunities and experiences available in cities outweigh the disadvantages. Others enjoy the fast pace and energy that cities provide.`nIn conclusion, living in a city has both advantages and disadvantages. The decision depends on individual preferences and priorities, as different people value different aspects of urban life.`n`nQuestions`n31. What is the main idea of the first paragraph?`nA. City life is perfect for everyoneB. Cities only offer advantagesC. Living in a city has both positive and negative aspectsD. People should avoid cities`n`n32. What is one benefit of living in a city mentioned in the text?`nA. Lower cost of livingB. Fewer job opportunitiesC. Greater access to employmentD. Less competition for jobs`n`n33. Why do some people find city life enjoyable?`nA. Because there are many activities and eventsB. Because cities are always quietC. Because people work lessD. Because life is slower`n`n34. What is one disadvantage related to money?`nA. Salaries are too lowB. Housing is expensiveC. Food is unavailableD. Transport is free`n`n35. What problem is mentioned about transport?`nA. Public transport is not availableB. Travel is always fastC. Traffic can be stressful and slowD. People do not travel`n`n36. What does the writer suggest in the conclusion?`nA. Everyone should live in citiesB. Cities are better than rural areasC. The choice depends on personal preferencesD. Cities will disappear in the future`n`nAnswer Key`nC `nC `nA `nB `nC `nC `n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'b170ab5a-f54f-4cae-ac2e-bd194181cafe', 'Text\nPart 6: Gapped Text`nYou are going to read an article about developing new hobbies. Six sentences have been removed from the article. Choose from the sentences A–G the one which fits each gap (31–36). There is one extra sentence which you do not need to use.`n`nText`nDiscovering New Hobbies`nTrying out new hobbies can be an exciting way to spend your free time and learn new skills. Many people, however, find it difficult to get started because they are unsure of what they might enjoy.`n(31) ______Sometimes, the best approach is simply to experiment with different activities until you find something that interests you. You might discover a passion you never expected.`nIt is important not to feel discouraged if you do not enjoy something straight away.(32) ______Giving yourself time to improve can make the experience more enjoyable.`nAnother useful idea is to learn from others. Joining a club or taking a class can provide valuable guidance and support.(33) ______Being part of a group can also make the activity more social and motivating.`nIn addition, hobbies do not need to be expensive or complicated. Many enjoyable activities require very little equipment or preparation.(34) ______Simple hobbies such as reading, drawing or walking can be just as rewarding.`nIt is also worth considering how much time you can realistically dedicate to your new hobby.(35) ______Choosing something that fits into your routine will make it easier to continue.`nFinally, remember that hobbies are meant to be enjoyable.(36) ______The goal is to relax and have fun, not to create unnecessary pressure.`n`nSentences`nA This allows you to meet people who share similar interests.B You should avoid choosing activities that require too much time.C In fact, many skills take time and practice to develop.D There is no need to become an expert immediately.E Some people worry about failing before they even begin.F As a result, it is important to choose something simple at first.G It is not necessary to spend a lot of money to get started.`n`nAnswer Key`n31 E32 C33 A34 G35 B36 D`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'b170ab5a-f54f-4cae-ac2e-bd194181cafe', 'Text\nPart 6: Gapped Text`nYou are going to read an article about the importance of learning new skills. Six sentences have been removed from the article. Choose from the sentences A–G the one which fits each gap (31–36). There is one extra sentence which you do not need to use.`n`nText`nWhy Learning Never Stops`nIn today’s fast-moving world, learning does not end when you leave school. In fact, many people continue to develop new skills throughout their lives.`n(31) ______This is because industries are constantly changing, and new technologies appear every year.`nFor many individuals, learning something new can feel challenging at first.(32) ______However, overcoming this fear is often the first step towards personal growth.`nOne effective way to learn is by setting clear and realistic goals.(33) ______Breaking a large goal into smaller steps makes the process more manageable.`nAnother useful strategy is to practise regularly.(34) ______Consistency is often more important than the amount of time spent learning.`nIn addition, it can be helpful to learn from others.(35) ______Sharing experiences and advice can make learning more enjoyable and effective.`nFinally, it is important to stay motivated.(36) ______Remembering why you started can help you continue even when progress seems slow.`n`nSentences`nA This helps learners stay focused and measure their progress.B Some people are afraid of making mistakes or failing.C For this reason, continuous learning has become essential.D Even a small amount of practice each day can lead to improvement.E Joining a group or finding a mentor can be very beneficial.F Motivation can sometimes decrease over time.G Not everyone enjoys studying in a traditional environment.`n`nAnswer Key`n31 C32 B33 A34 D35 E36 F`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'b170ab5a-f54f-4cae-ac2e-bd194181cafe', 'Text\nPart 6: Gapped Text`nYou are going to read an article about the benefits of working in a team. Six sentences have been removed from the article. Choose from the sentences A–G the one which fits each gap (31–36). There is one extra sentence which you do not need to use.`n`nText`nWorking Together Effectively`nIn many areas of life, from school projects to professional environments, teamwork plays a key role in achieving success. Working with others can bring many advantages, but it also requires certain skills.`n(31) ______When people collaborate, they can combine their strengths and produce better results than they would individually.`nHowever, teamwork is not always easy.(32) ______Differences in opinion can sometimes lead to conflict if they are not managed properly.`nFor this reason, good communication is essential.(33) ______Clear communication helps avoid misunderstandings and ensures that everyone understands their role.`nAnother important factor is trust.(34) ______Team members need to feel confident that others will complete their tasks on time.`nIn addition, it is important to respect different perspectives.(35) ______Being open to new ideas can improve the quality of the final result.`nFinally, successful teams often share a common goal.(36) ______This helps keep everyone motivated and focused on achieving the same objective.`n`nSentences`nA Without it, teamwork can quickly break down.B People may have different ideas about how to approach a task.C This allows for a wider range of solutions.D Everyone should have the chance to express their views.E A shared objective gives direction to the group.F As a result, working in a team can be highly productive.G It is important that all members communicate regularly.`n`nAnswer Key`n31 F32 B33 G34 A35 D36 E`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'b170ab5a-f54f-4cae-ac2e-bd194181cafe', 'Text\nB2 First (FCE) – Reading and Use of English`nPart 6: Gapped Text`nYou are going to read an article about developing healthy routines. Six sentences have been removed from the article. Choose from the sentences A–G the one which fits each gap (31–36). There is one extra sentence which you do not need to use.`n`nText`nBuilding Healthy Daily Habits`nCreating healthy daily habits can have a significant impact on your overall well-being. However, many people struggle to maintain routines over a long period of time.`n(31) ______Small, consistent actions are often more effective than making big changes all at once.`nAt the beginning, it is important to set realistic goals.(32) ______If your expectations are too high, you may feel discouraged and give up quickly.`nAnother key factor is consistency.(33) ______Repeating the same behaviour regularly helps turn it into a habit.`nIt can also be helpful to track your progress.(34) ______Seeing improvement over time can increase motivation and keep you focused.`nIn addition, your environment plays an important role.(35) ______For example, keeping healthy food visible can encourage better choices.`nFinally, it is essential to be patient.(36) ______Developing habits takes time, and results may not appear immediately.`n`nSentences`nA This is because habits are built gradually.B Making small changes is a good place to start.C Keeping a record can make your efforts more visible.D Your surroundings can influence your behaviour more than you think.E Doing something every day is more important than doing it perfectly.F Many people try to change everything at once and fail.G Setting goals that are too difficult can have negative effects.`n`nAnswer Key`n31 F32 G33 E34 C35 D36 A`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'b170ab5a-f54f-4cae-ac2e-bd194181cafe', 'Text\nPart 6: Gapped Text`nYou are going to read an article about the importance of taking breaks while studying. Six sentences have been removed from the article. Choose from the sentences A–G the one which fits each gap (31–36). There is one extra sentence which you do not need to use.`n`nText`nWhy Taking Breaks Improves Learning`nMany students believe that studying for long hours without stopping is the best way to achieve good results. However, research suggests that taking regular breaks can actually improve learning.`n(31) ______Short pauses during study sessions allow the brain to rest and process information more effectively.`nWithout breaks, it becomes harder to concentrate.(32) ______As a result, productivity often decreases over time.`nTaking breaks can also help reduce stress.(33) ______Stepping away from work for a few minutes can improve your mood and energy levels.`nAnother benefit is that breaks can increase creativity.(34) ______When you return to your work, you may find new solutions to problems.`nIt is important, however, to use breaks wisely.(35) ______Activities such as checking social media can easily take longer than planned.`nInstead, simple actions like stretching, walking or drinking water can be more effective.(36) ______These activities help refresh your mind without causing distractions.`n`nSentences`nA This is because the brain needs time to recover.B After a while, people may start to feel tired and lose focus.C Choosing the right type of break is essential.D A short rest can prevent feelings of frustration.E Changing your activity can help you see things differently.F For this reason, many experts recommend studying in shorter sessions.G They allow you to relax without losing too much time.`n`nAnswer Key`n31 F32 B33 D34 E35 C36 G`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'bd41d80c-bcdd-4ac9-9c06-13c2ab8fab6e', 'Text\nPart 7: Multiple Matching`nYou are going to read an article in which four people talk about their experiences of learning new skills. For questions 37–42, choose from the people (A–D). The people may be chosen more than once.`n`nWhich person…`n37 mentions feeling more confident after learning something new?38 found it difficult to stay motivated at the beginning?39 learned something mainly for professional reasons?40 enjoyed the social aspect of the experience?41 talks about improving slowly over time?42 mentions being surprised by their own ability?`n`nTexts`nA – Laura`nI decided to learn how to cook properly last year because I was tired of eating ready-made meals. At first, I found it quite challenging, especially because I made a lot of mistakes. However, I kept practising, and over time I noticed that my skills were improving little by little. Now I feel much more comfortable in the kitchen and even enjoy trying new recipes.`n`nB – Mark`nFor me, learning graphic design was something I needed for my job. My company expected me to develop these skills, so I didn’t really have a choice. Although I wasn’t very interested at first, I soon realised that I was actually quite good at it. That surprised me, and now I even use these skills for personal projects.`n`nC – Sofia`nI joined a photography class because I wanted to meet new people while doing something creative. The classes were fun, and I really enjoyed sharing ideas with others. It was great to be part of a group where everyone supported each other. As a result, I not only improved my photography but also made several good friends.`n`nD – James`nI started learning a new language a few months ago. In the beginning, I found it hard to stay motivated because progress seemed very slow. Sometimes I felt like giving up, but I decided to continue. Eventually, I began to understand more, and that gave me the confidence to keep going.`n`nAnswer Key`n37 D38 D39 B40 C41 A42 B`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'bd41d80c-bcdd-4ac9-9c06-13c2ab8fab6e', 'Text\nPart 7: Multiple Matching`nYou are going to read an article in which four people talk about their experiences of working from home. For questions 37–42, choose from the people (A–D). The people may be chosen more than once.`n`nWhich person…`n37 mentions saving time because of their situation?38 found it difficult to separate work and personal life?39 prefers their current situation to their previous one?40 mentions feeling lonely at times?41 talks about becoming more productive?42 had no choice about the change?`n`nTexts`nA – Daniel`nWhen my company decided that everyone had to work from home, I wasn’t very happy about it. I preferred going to the office, but there was nothing I could do. At first, it felt strange, but eventually I got used to it. Now I can see some advantages, although it wasn’t my decision to begin with.`n`nB – Emma`nWorking from home has made a huge difference to my daily routine. I no longer spend hours travelling to work, which gives me more time to relax or exercise. I feel much happier now than I did before, and I wouldn’t want to go back to my old schedule.`n`nC – Alex`nAt first, I thought working from home would be easy, but I quickly realised it wasn’t. I found it hard to stop working at the end of the day because everything happened in the same space. It was difficult to create clear boundaries between my job and my personal life.`n`nD – Sara`nOne thing I didn’t expect was how much I would miss being around other people. Although I can communicate with my colleagues online, it’s not the same as seeing them in person. On the positive side, I’ve noticed that I can concentrate better and get more work done.`n`nAnswer Key`n37 B38 C39 B40 D41 D42 A`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'bd41d80c-bcdd-4ac9-9c06-13c2ab8fab6e', 'Text\nPart 7: Multiple Matching`nYou are going to read an article in which four people talk about their experiences of practising sport regularly. For questions 37–42, choose from the people (A–D). The people may be chosen more than once.`n`nWhich person…`n37 says they didn’t enjoy the activity at the beginning?38 mentions that they needed encouragement to continue?39 talks about doing the activity for health reasons?40 says they have made new friends through the activity?41 mentions noticing gradual improvement?42 says they now feel more energetic?`n`nTexts`nA – Tom`nI started running because my doctor advised me to be more active. At first, I didn’t really like it and found it quite tiring. However, I kept going because I knew it was good for my health. After a few weeks, I began to feel fitter and had much more energy during the day.`n`nB – Lisa`nJoining a local yoga class was one of the best decisions I’ve made. Not only have I become more flexible, but I’ve also met some great people. We often talk after class, and sometimes we even meet outside the sessions. It has become both a social and relaxing activity for me.`n`nC – David`nWhen I first started going to the gym, I found it difficult to stay motivated. There were days when I wanted to give up, but my friend encouraged me to keep going. Thanks to that support, I didn’t quit. Over time, I noticed small improvements, which helped me stay focused.`n`nD – Anna`nSwimming has always been something I enjoyed, but I never took it seriously until recently. Now I go to the pool three times a week. I’ve seen my technique improve gradually, and I feel more confident in the water. It’s satisfying to see progress, even if it’s slow.`n`nAnswer Key`n37 A38 C39 A40 B41 D42 A`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'bd41d80c-bcdd-4ac9-9c06-13c2ab8fab6e', 'Text\nB2 First (FCE) – Reading and Use of English`nPart 7: Multiple Matching`nYou are going to read an article in which four people talk about their experiences of learning to play a musical instrument. For questions 37–42, choose from the people (A–D). The people may be chosen more than once.`n`nWhich person…`n37 mentions that progress was slow but satisfying?38 says they started for practical reasons?39 found it difficult to practise regularly?40 enjoyed performing in front of others?41 mentions help from another person?42 was surprised by how much they improved?`n`nTexts`nA – Kevin`nI decided to learn the guitar because I needed a hobby that would help me relax after work. At first, I didn’t practise as much as I should have, mainly because I was busy and often forgot. However, once I created a routine, I began to enjoy it more and improve steadily.`n`nB – Marta`nLearning the piano was not something I chose myself at the beginning. My parents wanted me to learn it when I was younger. Although I didn’t enjoy it much at first, I later realised how useful it was. I even performed at a school concert, which I found exciting.`n`nC – Luis`nWhen I started playing the violin, I found it quite difficult and progress was slow. However, each small improvement felt like an achievement. Over time, I became more confident and proud of what I could do.`n`nD – Rachel`nI began learning the drums with the help of a friend who already knew how to play. He showed me the basics and encouraged me when I felt stuck. I didn’t expect to improve so quickly, but after a few months I realised I had made much more progress than I thought.`n`nAnswer Key`n37 C38 B39 A40 B41 D42 D`n', now());
insert into public.levels_preguntas (id, examen_id, level_id, parte_id, enunciado, creado_en) values (gen_random_uuid(), 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'ae0e85e8-3d63-11f1-b2e3-0b27f7b23431', 'bd41d80c-bcdd-4ac9-9c06-13c2ab8fab6e', 'Text\nPart 7: Multiple Matching`nYou are going to read an article in which four people talk about their experiences of travelling alone. For questions 37–42, choose from the people (A–D). The people may be chosen more than once.`n`nWhich person…`n37 mentions feeling nervous before starting?38 says the experience helped them become more independent?39 had a negative experience at some point?40 enjoyed having complete control over their plans?41 mentions meeting new people during the trip?42 says they would repeat the experience?`n`nTexts`nA – Julia`nBefore my first solo trip, I felt quite anxious because I had never travelled alone before. However, once I arrived, I realised I could manage everything by myself. By the end of the trip, I felt much more independent and confident in my abilities.`n`nB – Carlos`nTravelling alone gave me the freedom to decide exactly what I wanted to do each day. I didn’t have to compromise with anyone, which I really enjoyed. I could change my plans whenever I wanted, and that made the experience very relaxing.`n`nC – Hannah`nDuring my trip, I stayed in several hostels, which made it easy to meet other travellers. We shared stories, explored places together and even stayed in touch afterwards. It was one of the most social experiences I’ve ever had.`n`nD – Liam`nAlthough I generally enjoyed travelling alone, there was one moment when I got lost in an unfamiliar city and felt quite stressed. Despite that, I learned a lot from the experience, and I would definitely consider doing it again in the future.`n`nAnswer Key`n37 A38 A39 D40 B41 C42 D`n', now());
